  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "b2Lfcd78Kk/zxB9mH/IdY/9vbQo=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:13.190Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "VNG Realisatie belongs to the association of Dutch municipalities and owns Common Ground and the FSC standard. That ownership is the claim: every supplier selling into Dutch municipal government has to conform to an architecture this body defines.\n\nIt follows that VNG is an influence target rather than a delivery channel. Winning a project with a supplier affects one municipality; affecting what Common Ground or FSC requires affects the constraint every supplier in the market builds against. That is the highest-leverage and the slowest position available in the Dutch track.\n\nIt also explains why several other Dutch entries in this set are valuable partly through their proximity to this body \u2014 co-developing standards with VNG recurs as a qualifying signal. The priority-3 placement reflects the length of the cycle rather than the size of the prize.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- VNG Realisatie (NL)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Association of Dutch Municipalities; owns Common Ground and the FSC standard. \u2014 Sets the architecture every Dutch municipal supplier must conform to. Influence target.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:29:13.190192Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:13.190196Z"
    }
  },
